  answer: Chayce uses its own DBS-checked team, holds goods in transit and public liability insurance, and sets out the insurance cover in the service agreement before any move begins.
  answerMore: Clients, and the family members helping them, can contact us by phone or email, including to make a complaint.
faqs:
- q: Are Chayce&rsquo;s staff DBS-checked?
  a: Yes. The people who work in clients&rsquo; homes for Chayce are DBS-checked to Enhanced level, including the barred list check. A DBS check is a criminal record check carried out through the Disclosure and Barring Service, which covers England and Wales.
- q: Is my move insured?
  a: Every removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit. Chayce holds goods in transit insurance and public liability insurance, with details set out in the service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Can a family member arrange a move on behalf of a parent?
  a: Yes, many of our clients are helped by their children. If someone holds a Lasting Power of Attorney or is helping to make decisions, please tell us at the start so that decisions are made by the right person.
- q: How do you collect reviews?
  a: We invite every client to leave an honest review on Google or Trustpilot. We never pay for reviews, offer anything in return for them, or write them ourselves, and we never ask anyone to change or remove an honest review.
- q: How do I make a complaint?
  a: Tell us as soon as you can by phone on 07708 925432 or by email at info@chayceproperties.com. We will look into what happened and tell you what we will do about it.
